hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24073","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his grandfather, the grandfather of Said: What is your name? He said: Hazn. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather you are Sahl. He said: I will not change a name my father named me. Ibn al-Musayyab said: So roughness remained in us afterwards."
"24074","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, he said: When death attended Abu Talib, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon him, and with him were Abu Jahl and Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah. So he said: O uncle, say: There is no god but Allah, a word I will argue for you with before Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So Abu Jahl and Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah said: O Abu Talib, do you turn away from the religion of Abd al-Muttalib? He said: So they kept speaking to him until the last thing he spoke to them with was: upon the religion of Abd al-Muttalib. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will surely seek forgiveness for you while I am not forbidden from you. So it was revealed: It is not for the Prophet and those who believed to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they are kin, after it became clear to them that they are companions of Hell. He said: So it was revealed concerning him: You do not guide whom you love."
"24075","Narrated to us Affan, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Tariq, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: My father was among those who pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under the tree, the pledge of al-Ridwan. So he said: We went in the next year as pilgrims, and its place was obscured to us. If it became clear to you, then you know best."
"24076","Narrated to us Abu Ahmad, narrated to us Sufyan, from Tariq, he said: The tree was mentioned to Said ibn al-Musayyab, so he said: My father narrated to me that he was that year with them, and they forgot it the next year."
